# E02 BDI Architecture: sequential, fixed order, no random draw, so the C# guarantees the order of every line (exact
# trace, level (a)). 120 turns (the oracle bounds noTurns, tests/tools/csharp-ref), delay 0. "order" checks how the kinds of
# line interleave, the other facts their contents in sequence: together, the whole trace.
cover all
fact order ^(Starting|\t\[[\w-]+ -> [\w-]+\]|Adopting|GUI)
fact start ^Starting (\w+)$
fact message ^\t\[([\w-]+) -> ([\w-]+)\]: (.*)$
fact intention ^Adopting new intention: (.*)$
fact gui ^GUI pos=(\d+) ([.FWw]+)$
same order seq
same start seq
same message seq
same intention seq
same gui seq
# the terrain refreshes its form once per turn after the setup turn
check gui count == 119
# no exception caught by an agent (the form of the C# drawn before its thread has created it, an access out of the
# terrain): neither output may hold one
fact error (Object reference|out of range|Index was|Exception)
optional error
check error count == 0
